sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Caller
    participant Gateway as API Gateway (HTTP)
    participant Ticket as Ticket Service (gRPC)
    participant Department as Department Service (REST)
    participant DB as Ticket SQLite
    participant Stub as Notification log stub

    Caller->>Gateway: POST /tickets/:id/assign + x-request-id
    Gateway->>Ticket: AssignTicket + metadata ID + native deadline (3s)
    Ticket->>DB: Load ticket and validate allowed state
    Ticket->>Department: GET /departments/:id + same ID<br/>timeout min(2s, remaining deadline - margin)
    alt Department unreachable
        Department--xTicket: Connection failure
        Ticket-->>Gateway: UNAVAILABLE (no writes)
        Gateway-->>Caller: HTTP 503 + x-request-id
    else Department lookup exceeds budget
        Ticket->>Ticket: Abort fetch and stop lookup
        Ticket-->>Gateway: DEADLINE_EXCEEDED (no writes)
        Gateway-->>Caller: HTTP 504 + x-request-id
    else Department missing
        Department-->>Ticket: HTTP 404
        Ticket-->>Gateway: NOT_FOUND (no writes)
        Gateway-->>Caller: HTTP 404 + x-request-id
    else Department valid
        Department-->>Ticket: HTTP 200 + department
        Ticket->>Ticket: Check cancellation/deadline before saving
        Ticket->>DB: Transaction: ticket ASSIGNED + history
        DB-->>Ticket: Commit
        Ticket->>Stub: Log notification
        Ticket-->>Gateway: ASSIGNED ticket
        Gateway-->>Caller: HTTP 200 + x-request-id
    end

    Note over Caller,DB: A deadline after commit can leave an uncertain result.<br/>Read ticket/history before another mutation.<br/>Automatic mutation retries are disabled.
    Note over Ticket,Stub: RabbitMQ/Notification Service is target work.<br/>This implemented flow still uses the log stub.
